+## Bounded peer learnability check — 2026-10-24
+
+**New finite witness: a bounding-box-area ranking rival fits four visible examples and fails the query.** On unchanged generator SHA-256 `e5207a349a9fb541e5436005a192f893597a320888a1510c0f6f9d8ff7b3080f`, medium seed 12, consecutive sample indices 0–3 give four demonstrations on which sorting objects by bounding-box area descending (ties by top-left), instead of occupied-cell area descending, predicts exactly the executed protected Racket labels. Sample index 4 distinguishes them: header count 3 selects the color-4 body with occupied area 4 under the intended rule, producing `[[8,8,8],[0,0,8]]`; the rival instead selects the color-8 horizontal body with bounding-box area 5 and predicts `[[8,8,8,8,8]]`. Body occupied/bounding-box areas are respectively color 8: 5/5, color 7: 3/4, color 6: 6/8, color 4: 4/6.
+
